>I had a +3 pair of speed boots.  I read a blessed scroll of enchant armor,
>after which they became +5.  When they did, I also got the message, "Your
>pair of speed boots suddenly vibrates unexpectedly."  They didn't vanish,
>and they still appear to function normally.  What caused this message?
>-- 

It is indeed a warning, and I've also noticed it. This means they
have changed the enchantment rules in NH3.1, because in NH3.0 it was always
possible to enchant armor if it was +3 or less. For weapons this used to 
be save if they were +5 or less, which meant you could always enchant them
to +8 with a blessed scroll of enchant weapon. 
From experience (I didn't look in the source) I would say that both
weapons and armor have a chance of getting destroyed if the enchantment
gets them higher then +3.
They also changed the effect of blessed scrolls of enchant weapon,
these used to give +3 (always), now it's something between +1 and +3.

I don't mind the weapon part of this, a +5 Excalibur is good enough
to win the game. But the extra chance of your armor getting destroyed
is nasty.

